      "name": "technical_depth",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Categorises the diagnostic effort a ticket requires, a strong new axis directly predictive of resolution time. Values are sound readings: CS-0002's config push maps to config_troubleshooting, CS-0003's 502 outage to system_investigation. Well-distributed, not near-constant."
    },
    {
      "name": "scope_span",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Blast radius (single account vs multiple tenants) is a plausible driver of resolution effort and gives a genuine grouping axis. Values are well grounded: CS-0003 explicitly names the Acme tenant with all members affected, mapped reasonably (though 'multiple_tenants' is a slight stretch from a single tenant). Good variance."
    },
    {
      "name": "outage_scale",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Severity of outage is relevant to urgency and effort. Grounded well: CS-0003 production 502 outage correctly flagged; CS-0004 feature request correctly Unknown/NULL. Some overlap with technical_depth/scope but retains distinct severity signal. Default 'single_workflow_broken' on the billing-invoice CS-0001 is a mild over-assertion of an outage where none exists."
    },
    {
      "name": "requires_engineering",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Whether code/deployment change is needed is a strong predictor of long resolution and distinct from technical_depth. Mostly grounded, but some inferences are shaky: CS-0003's active outage labelled 'investigation_only_no_code_change' and CS-0004's feature request labelled 'code_or_deployment_change' are defensible but not clearly supported by the text."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_feature_request",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A binary flag but a meaningful one: feature requests behave differently from bugs in resolution dynamics, so it offers real grouping leverage. Values well grounded — CS-0004 correctly True, others False."
    },
    {
      "name": "diagnostics_provided",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Quality of supplied diagnostics is a credible driver of faster/slower resolution and a good new axis. Grounded: CS-0002 provides browser/OS repro details -> reproduction_steps_provided; CS-0001 lacks logs -> insufficient. Reasonable readings."
    },
    {
      "name": "ambiguity_level",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Clarity of the request is plausibly linked to resolution time and provides a distinct axis from diagnostics. Heavily skewed toward 'clearly_stated_with_context' (190/250) but still has usable variance. Sample values are sound readings of the source text."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.87,
  "source_groundedness": 0.84,
  "rationale": "All seven added columns give genuine, differentiated axes for modelling resolution time — technical depth, blast radius, outage severity, engineering need, request type, diagnostics quality, and ambiguity. None are near-constant or trivial restatements, though outage_scale/requires_engineering/technical_depth share some conceptual overlap. Values are generally sound categorisations of the issue text, with correct NULL/Unknown behaviour on silent rows. Minor over-assertions appear (default 'single_workflow_broken' on a non-outage billing ticket, a single-tenant case labelled 'multiple_tenants', and some engineering-need inferences), but no systematic hallucination. Overall high quality on both necessary conditions."
